==== Exact scaling C' : T^2 = octic(t) ====
  w^4+16u^2v^2 - q^8*octic(p/q) = 0
  (expect 0) ==> T := g/(w q^4) satisfies  T^2 = octic(t).  This is C'.

==== Exact scaling C'_pal : S^2 = W^4+64W^2-256 ====
  octic - t^4*(W^4+64W^2-256) = 0
  (expect 0) ==> S := T/t^2 satisfies S^2 = W^4+64W^2-256.

==== End-to-end numeric sanity on a genuine Saunderson value ====
  Saunderson(3,4,5) brick = (117,44,240)
  a^2+b^2+c^2 = 73225  is square : 0
  octic(t=2) = 2929
  W = t+1/t = 5/2,  W^4+64W^2-256 = 2929/16
  W^2-4 = 9/4 = (t-1/t)^2 = 9/4
  T0 = t-1/t = 3/2,  T0^4+72T0^2+16 = 2929/16 is square : 0
  (this is the NON-degenerate brick (44,117,240); body diagonal is NOT a square,
   consistent with: the corresponding C0-point would need T0 nonzero, impossible.)

